    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Discuss the role of any two factors influencing population change.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The birth rate and the death rate are two factors that influence population change. The birth rate is the number of live births per 1000 people, while the death rate is the number of deaths per 1000 people. When the birth rate is higher than the death rate, population increases; when the death rate exceeds the birth rate, population decreases.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, the balance between birth and death rates determines population change.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
